<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Temryukovna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1544–<a href="/years/1569">1569</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Temryukovna was a Kabardian princess, the daughter of Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temryuk-idarov">Temryuk of Kabarda</a>, who was baptised and married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV of Russia</a> in 1561 as his second wife. The marriage sealed Kabarda's alliance with Muscovy and brought Kabardian princely families into the Russian nobility. She died in 1569, and her brother Mikhail Cherkassky rose high at the Muscovite court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-temryukovna.jpg" alt="Maria Temryukovna" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shahiiiyhh · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMG_mahidevran_sultan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
